INT. ROSIE'S DINER - BOOTH BY THE WINDOW - NIGHT

A half-empty diner. A neon sign BUZZES in the window. Three strangers sit at one booth, three phones face-up on the table, none of them quite looking at each other, a plate of cold fries in the middle that nobody has touched, a waitress refilling coffee two booths over.

CLOSE ON the middle phone. A group chat. "nightowls_3am" glowing at the top.

WE SEE the last message, from "moth": "ok so who's actually here."

MAYA
(turns her phone over, then back)
so. um. i'm maya.

DESMOND
(leaning back, arms crossed)
desmond. i'm "moth."

MAYA
(small laugh)
you're moth? you type like a forty year old.

DESMOND
(a shrug)
i am a forty year old.

The waitress sets down a coffee. Leaves. A beat.

THEO
(pushing the fries a half inch toward them)
i didn't think anyone would actually show up.

MAYA
you set the time, theo.

THEO
(eyes on the table)
yeah. i know.

DESMOND
so you're "lantern."

THEO
yeah.

MAYA
the one who said he found something in the old church.

THEO
(a pause)
it was a long time ago.

DESMOND
it was last tuesday.

A phone BUZZES on the table. Everyone looks. It's Maya's. She doesn't pick it up.

MAYA
(flips it face down)
it's my mom.

DESMOND
you can get it.

MAYA
(a thin smile)
no, it's fine.

ANGLE ON Theo's hand, tapping the table. Tap. Tap. Tap.

THEO
(too quiet)
i didn't find anything. i wrote it. the whole thing. i made it up.

MAYA
(a beat, then, steady)
okay.

DESMOND
(sits forward)
why?

THEO
(shrugs, can't look up)
i wanted someone to message back.

Silence. The neon BUZZES. A truck HISSES past outside.

MAYA
(slides the fries closer)
eat something, lantern.

THEO
(a breath)
it's theo.

MAYA
i know.

DESMOND
(picks up one fry, studies it)
these are terrible.

THEO
(a short laugh, surprised at itself)
yeah.

The three of them sit. Desmond eats the fry. Maya reaches over and takes one. Theo, after a moment, takes the last.

A door SLAMS somewhere in the back. All three flinch. Nobody says anything.

BACK TO SCENE

The waitress comes by. Tops off the coffees. Looks at the three of them, then at the fries.

DESMOND
(to the waitress)
can we get another plate of those?

The waitress nods. Goes. The phones on the table light up at once, three at a time, the group chat filling with messages from people who aren't here.

MAYA
(reading)
"is everyone ok"

DESMOND
(typing, slowly, two fingers)
"we're good."

THEO
(watching him)
you're still typing like a forty year old.

DESMOND
(without looking up)
it's a gift.
